{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.322, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2323}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2323, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8613, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 987, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_0174rEeMqMEHrsvP72jqkGo8", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters. dSph gamma-ray limits: one-sided 95% upper limit at 2Δln L = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, i.e. 1.355 in ln L) below the maximum. The nuisance parameter is each dwarf's J-factor, via the normalization s (J = sJ0) with a Gaussian log10 prior, profiled over log10 s in [-3,3]. AMS-02 antiproton limits: upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region (Q = -2 ln L). The nuisance parameter is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197), profiled over 1–12 kpc. The paper says 3.84 differs from the common one-sided 2.71 prescription that the dSph analysis uses.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T075045Z_dev-02_staged_eb9f", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters. dSph gamma-ray limits: one-sided 95% upper limit at 2Δln L = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, i.e. 1.355 in ln L) below the maximum. The nuisance parameter is each dwarf's J-factor, via the normalization s (J = sJ0) with a Gaussian log10 prior, profiled over log10 s in [-3,3]. AMS-02 antiproton limits: upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region (Q = -2 ln L). The nuisance parameter is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197), profiled over 1–12 kpc. The paper says 3.84 differs from the common one-sided 2.71 prescription that the dSph analysis uses.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 10.887, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1307, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2323, "cache_read_input_tokens": 23044, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T07:50:56+00:00"}
